steps.prompt:
The chat should show visuals the agent asks for, drawn with the design system’s flow and map components (components/flow.html, and components/map.html with its .touched, .proposed and .named markers), following D-v3x, “Agents draw visuals as fenced blocks in a small versioned vocabulary”. Design how they look in the transcript:

- a flow in the agent’s message, and a map with the parts a change touched;
- several visuals in one message, mixed with text;
- a block Prelude couldn’t read, shown as the agent wrote it, with a quiet note saying why;
- a narrow chat column and the pop-out window;
- while the agent is still writing the block.

Build Design Workspace’s visuals in the chat, following D-v3x:

- the parser and checker in visuals (server/visuals.js);
- one Eta partial per visual under server/views/, rendering components/flow.html and components/map.html unchanged;
- the vocabulary in the agent’s prompts in server/agent.js, for every kind whose rules say it may draw (R-4hd);
- --series-1 to --series-5, .flow and the map markers ported to ds/v1.

Unreadable blocks fall back as R-t2w says. Add tests for the parser: a good flow, an unknown part, a bad format, an unfinished block mid-stream.
